    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "I saw actually that debate, which was, I guess, originally on C-Span. And there was the bone of contention, which also kind of is similar in the Farm Bill of, if you've got a felony, you can't come in. Now, in this Farm Bill, you can come in after 10 years or something like that. What are your thoughts on that kind of, you know, kind of pushing folks out because they've maybe made some mistakes in the past, right off the bat, as opposed to kind of bringing them in once they've, what, how to come to Jesus' moment, so to speak. I'll say to you.",
