  {
    "episode_id": 94311,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94311.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 48,
    "turn_text": "that I think a lot of people take the short view and for a lot of people, it's about, well, what does this mean for the next election? I don't think that type of mentality is conducive to building a stronger, healthier, and more prosperous society. It's just like a lot of colleagues on the immigration issue. Oh, well, if we grant all these people citizenship, they're all going to vote against us. That's not true, especially if we're the ones who voted to allow them the opportunity to legalize and eventually to become citizens, some of them might actually appreciate that. And I'm just a lot more sober about these things. I think whether it's ex-fallens or whether it's immigrants, once they are welcomed into society, they're probably going to distribute somewhat normally on the bell curve. There we go. kind of work they do, how they vote, where they live. So I think we have to take the long view and say, well, let's stop worrying about the next two years. Let's think about the next 10, 15, 20 years. We're at a great disadvantage that Chinese think in terms of the next 50 years. And of course, They have some advantages that I don't want us to have. They don't have real elections and they have a dictatorship and they don't respect human rights. But I think we can with those caveats. Exactly. I think we can. mature and realize that, you know, thinking about the next six months and about the next year is really no way to manage a country, the greatest country in the world. And right now we have a lot of people who are excluded from our society because they made what were regarded back then, mistakes increasingly. Marijuana possession is not a state crime at least throughout our country. There we go. So",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Many people adopt a short-term perspective when making policy decisions.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Marijuana possession is not a state crime in most parts of the United States.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "For many people, political decisions are driven by concerns about the next election.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "A short-term mindset is not conducive to building a stronger, healthier, and more prosperous society.",
        "confidence": 0.93
